# --- Remote 3D models (Azure Blob Storage + Azure CDN) ---------------------
#
# Base URL of the container that hosts ALL 3D assets — both the GLB models
# (GlbModel.tsx) AND the Poly Haven .gltf texture sets (materials/pbr.tsx). When
# set, they load from `${VITE_MODELS_BASE_URL}/<path>` instead of the bundled
# copies in public/models. Leave it unset (or delete the line) to use the local
# files — handy for offline dev. A trailing slash is optional.
#
# Heads-up: the PBR textures are *essential* startup assets that gate the loading
# screen, so a remote base means first paint waits on those fetches — use a fast,
# edge-cached CDN.
#
# Must be VITE_-prefixed: Vite only exposes VITE_* env vars to client code.
#
# Setup on Azure:
#   1. Upload the entire public/models tree to a Blob container (e.g. "models") —
#      every *.glb AND the *.gltf/textures/ folders, preserving the paths.
#   2. Put Azure CDN (or Front Door) in front of the storage account.
#   3. Add a CORS rule on the storage account / Blob service:
#         Allowed origins:  https://<your-static-web-app-domain>  (and http://localhost:5173 for dev)
#         Allowed methods:  GET, HEAD
#         Allowed headers:  *
#         Max age:          3600
#   4. Set Content-Type per blob: "model/gltf-binary" for *.glb, "image/jpeg" for
#      the texture .jpg files, "image/x-exr" (or application/octet-stream) for .exr.
#
# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in your real endpoint:
VITE_MODELS_BASE_URL=https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net/models

# Base URL of the container hosting the HDRI/.exr environment map
# (materials/SceneEnvironment.tsx). Same Azure storage account + CORS rule as
# above; just a different container/folder. Unset → bundled copy in public/hdri.
# The .exr is loaded for image-based lighting; it is NOT on the loading-screen
# critical path, so a remote base here only delays reflections settling in.
VITE_HDRI_BASE_URL=https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net/hdri
